ges/2020/10/5/videoboard.jpg" /><br /><br />Arizona Game Information]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2020/10/5/videoboard.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2020/10/5/videoboard.jpg"><media:title>North Videoboard</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2020/10/5/videoboard.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:30:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59497</s:story_id></item><item><title>Big 12 Fall Tour Comes to Morgantown</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/6/football-big-12-fall-tour-comes-to-morgantown</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/6/football-big-12-fall-tour-comes-to-morgantown</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Big12Tour-26" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/6/Big_12_Fall_Tour_1920x1080.png" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va.  – The Big 12 Conference's Fall Tour makes a stop in Morgantown on Oct. 8- 10. As the host university, WVU will choose a local school to receive an upgrade to a STEM center or a library, courtesy of the College Football Playoff Foundation's Extra Yard for Teachers Makeover Project. Other events include an Empowerment Luncheon on Friday, and a tailgate and pregame concert designed to further enhance the game-day experience across the Big 12 schools on Saturday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/6/Big_12_Fall_Tour_1920x1080.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/6/Big_12_Fall_Tour_1920x1080.png"><media:title>Big12Tour-26</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/6/Big_12_Fall_Tour_1920x1080.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:33:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59496</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Athletics and the Mountaineer Athletic Club Launch New Giving Initiative – Champions Circle</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/6/general-wvu-athletics-and-the-mountaineer-athletic-club-launch-new-giving-initiative-champions-circle</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/6/general-wvu-athletics-and-the-mountaineer-athletic-club-launch-new-giving-initiative-champions-circle</guid><category>General</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="MAC26_Champions Circle_1024x576" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/6/ChampionsCircleAnnouncement_1024x576.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. — The Mountaineer Athletic Club (MAC) and WVU Athletics announced the launch of the Champions Circle, a new giving initiative created to support the Championship Resource Fund. Champions Circle members play a key role in advancing WVU Athletics' mission through their philanthropic giving above and beyond ticketing and seating contributions.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/6/ChampionsCircleAnnouncement_1024x576.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/6/ChampionsCircleAnnouncement_1024x576.jpg"><media:title>MAC26_Champions Circle_1024x576</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;imag